# release=2. The 3.24.43-1 that was published has no .PKGINFO in it - the
# archive is corrupt, publish-pkgs.sh skips it, and scraps cannot install it,
# which is why anything needing GTK fell back to a source build. A rebuilt
# -1 would be the same name with different bytes, which publishing refuses,
# so the fix carries a new release. Without this marker gen-ports.py rewrites
# the recipe from the manifest and puts release back to 1.
